    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0364" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/10</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-07T23:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 8, 5 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>299. Your August 5, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d115-f1"/> I have delivered
                    directly to the King the message of the President. His Majesty expressed most
                    earnestly his thanks and requested me to convey them to the President. He talked
                    long and appreciatively and he expressed the hope that an occasion would come
                    when the President’s offer of mediation might be accepted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
